Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.00,Header,,0,0,0,,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.78,0:00:06.14,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,1250,4620,5340)\pos(643.337,401.642)}Episode 63\N\N\N\N\NThe Burning of the Linked Camps
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.77,0:00:10.36,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,Liu Bei's troops, with great momentum, reached Xiaoting.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.36,0:00:13.35,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,Everyone in the Southlands trembled in fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.35,0:00:17.22,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Sun Quan, the Marquis of Wu, \Nseized Fan Qiang and Zhang Da,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.22,0:00:23.08,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and sent them back with Zhang Fei's head \Nand a request to sue for peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.63,0:00:48.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy Eastern Wu!\NSatiate the loyal souls with blood!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.12,0:00:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,671.642)\bord13.746}Your Majesty, as the offenders have been captured,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.21,0:00:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,671.642)\bord13.746}the dead have been avenged.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.64,0:01:00.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Cheng Bing of Eastern Wu is here to offer the return of Jing Province and Lady Sun
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.92,0:01:04.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.433}in order to forge an eternal\N alliance to destroy Wei together.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.24,0:01:06.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,671.642)\bord13.746}I await your imperial order.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.82,0:01:09.30,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(989.804,446.667)}Liú Bèi\NStyled: Xuándé
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.72,0:01:13.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,671.642)\bord13.746}Sun Quan is my most hated enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.94,0:01:17.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,671.642)\bord13.746}Should we forge an alliance with him,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.28,0:01:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,671.642)\bord13.746}I would betray the Oath of the Peach Garden.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.29,0:01:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.433}Our mind is set: Destroy Wu first, then Wei!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.50,0:01:27.94,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(300.145,476.001)}Sūn Quán\NStyled: Zhòngmóu
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.94,0:01:31.34,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(355.586,485.334)}Chéng Bǐng\NStyled: Déshū
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.58,0:01:28.26,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.26,0:01:31.67,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Liu Bei refused to make peace and\N swore to avenge his brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.67,0:01:34.64,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He wishes to destroy Wu first, then Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.64,0:01:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,His officials remonstrated against this, \Nbut Liu Bei did not listen. What should be done?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.81,0:01:46.45,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, Wu is in peril. Please make a decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.82,0:01:48.22,Default,,0,0,0,,A decision must be made.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.22,0:01:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Is sitting and waiting for death the only option for us?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.52,0:02:00.98,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3280,3440)\pos(967.619,480)}Kàn Zé\NStyled: Dérùn
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.06,0:02:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}My lord, there is a sky-holding\N pillar by your side. Why not use him?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.65,0:02:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Oh? Who do you speak of?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.95,0:02:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Lu Xun, Lu Boyan.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.16,0:02:17.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}In the past, everything was \Ndelegated to Zhou the Youth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.09,0:02:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Then, Lu Zijing replaced him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.99,0:02:21.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}After Zijing passed away, Lü Meng made decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.62,0:02:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Now though Lü Meng has passed, \N we still have Lu Xun at Jing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.30,0:02:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Though he may seem like a bookworm, \Nhe has great talent in strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.90,0:02:31.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}In my opinion, he is no lesser than Zhou the Youth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.94,0:02:35.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}The defeat of Guan Yu was all due to Lu Xun.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.62,0:02:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Should you use him, the Shu armies will be defeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.00,0:02:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}If any failures occur, I am willing to share the guilt.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.97,0:02:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Your wisdom prevented me from erring!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.10,0:02:58.99,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,My lord, Lu Xun is but a simple scholar.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.99,0:03:02.71,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He is no match for Liu Bei. \NI fear that he cannot be assigned.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.55,0:03:09.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Lu Xun is young and lacks prestige.\N I fear that our fellow gentry will not accept him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.20,0:03:12.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Thus, chaos will ensue and hasten our doom.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.02,0:03:17.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Lu Xun's talents are only in managing a commandery.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.06,0:03:20.24,Default,,0,0,0,,To have him manage state affairs is inadvisable.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.76,0:03:21.76,Default,,0,0,0,,That...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.76,0:03:25.42,Default,,0,0,0,,If you do not use Lu Xun, then Wu will be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.93,0:03:31.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear this with the lives of my entire family.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.86,0:03:48.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4300,4700)\pos(973.512,446.587)}Lù Xùn\NStyled: Bóyán
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.67,0:04:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I hereby appoint Lu Xun as Chief-Commander,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.00,0:04:05.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Right Protector-General, and\N General who Guards the West.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.22,0:04:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}He is given the title of Marquis of Lou, \N a sword, seal, and ribbon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.82,0:04:12.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}He shall command the troops of the \Nsix commanderies as well as those of Jingchu.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.28,0:04:15.30,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.29,0:04:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Within city walls shall I lead;
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.15,0:04:28.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}outside them shall you take command.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.18,0:04:50.02,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3500,3820)\pos(318.991,464)}Hán Dāng\NStyled: Yìgōng
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.56,0:04:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is our lord sending a\Nmere pedant to marshal the troops?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.26,0:04:57.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is their new Commander?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.03,0:04:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Lu Xun, Lu Boyan.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.42,0:05:00.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh? Him?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.89,0:05:05.04,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,With a bookworm as our commander, how can we win?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.04,0:05:06.33,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Let's see how he leads.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.33,0:05:09.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Quit yapping. Prepare to welcome the Commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.24,0:05:10.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.86,0:05:16.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3500,3820)\pos(478.611,508)}Mǎ Liáng\NStyled: Jìcháng
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.29,0:05:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of a man is Lu Xun?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.82,0:05:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}He is a scholar of Eastern Wu in name,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.78,0:05:22.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}but he has been talented since\N his youth and strategizes well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.06,0:05:25.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}It was he who orchestrated the seizure of Jing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.81,0:05:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}That whelp murdered my second brother; we are here just in time to catch him!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.01,0:05:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Your Majesty, his talent is \Nno less than that of Zhou the Youth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.42,0:05:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Do not underestimate him!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.00,0:05:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I led armies for years, yet I am beneath a kid?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.15,0:05:46.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.433}We have 750,000 troops and forty\N camps set seven hundred {\i1}li{\i0} in length.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.04,0:05:47.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}What can he do to us?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.24,0:05:53.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Pass my edict:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.40,0:05:55.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Attack all passes, fords, and chokepoints!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.36,0:05:56.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.50,0:06:00.74,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(298.487,457.333)}Zhōu Tài\NStyled: Yòupíng
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.68,0:06:02.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, the Marquis' nephew and\N General who Pacifies the East, Sun Huan,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.32,0:06:03.95,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,is trapped inside Yiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.95,0:06:05.97,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He has neither supplies or support.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.97,0:06:11.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, please rescue Sun Huan \Nsoon and ease the Marquis's mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.78,0:06:14.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that Sun Huan is popular among his men.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.31,0:06:17.07,Default,,0,0,0,,He can endure; there is no need to rescue him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.07,0:06:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.53,0:06:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,After I defeat Shu, he will naturally leave the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.69,0:06:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, please allocate troops against the enemy!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.82,0:06:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, please give your orders. \NWe are willing to fight to the death!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.58,0:06:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Your orders, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.50,0:06:38.45,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Generals, starting now, \Nyou will return to your garrisons,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.45,0:06:41.29,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,fortify your camps, and defend the chokepoints well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.50,0:06:44.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless otherwise ordered, do not sally forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.22,0:06:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Dismissed!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.49,0:06:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Look!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.54,0:06:59.46,Default,,0,0,0,,With this rascal as our general, Eastern Wu is ruined!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.46,0:07:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I tried to get an answer, but he has not a single plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.74,0:07:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,How can we ever defeat Shu?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.48,0:07:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,A yellow canopy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.18,0:07:16.24,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,General, I can faintly see a \Nyellow canopy on the mountain!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.24,0:07:19.13,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Clearly Liu Bei is here to scout the camp!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.68,0:07:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,-Gather the men and sally forth!\N-Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.15,0:07:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.84,0:07:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,-Hurry and inform the Commander.\N-Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.38,0:07:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you going, General Han?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.34,0:07:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei's scouts are here. I am sallying forth!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.45,0:07:54.12,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I am here on the King's orders. \NI urged you yesterday to defend chokepoints.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.12,0:07:56.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Nevertheless, you disobey me. Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.26,0:08:00.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}I pacified Jiangnan with General Sun Jian, \Nfighting in hundreds of battles.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.26,0:08:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}The others followed the General who Attacks Rebels
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.24,0:08:03.24,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: The general refers to Sun Ce.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.24,0:08:05.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}or the current King of Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.20,0:08:08.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}We are all warriors who \Nheld weapons and risked death.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.53,0:08:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Now that the Emperor made you the Chief-Commander,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.03,0:08:14.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}a plan must be made to repel the Shu troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.16,0:08:17.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Ours is to advance and lead the troops to victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.98,0:08:20.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Yet now, you order us to stay put.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.26,0:08:23.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Are we to expect Heaven to smite them for us?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.99,0:08:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,General Han is right! We are not men who fear death!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.05,0:08:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,We are willing to fight to our last!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.73,0:08:38.38,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Though I am but a scholar, the King has entrusted me with an important task.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.52,0:08:41.74,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,You must defend chokepoints and guard strongholds.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.78,0:08:44.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not strike out!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.03,0:08:46.75,Default,,0,0,0,,We are willing to fight to our last!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.75,0:08:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the King's sword! Those who defy my orders will be executed!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.68,0:09:15.10,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei, the Lord of Shu, stood off against Lu Xun, the Chief-Commander of Eastern Wu, at Yiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.10,0:09:18.23,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Lu Xun, declining to fight, waited for an opportunity.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.69,0:09:24.02,Thinking,,0,0,0,,The Shu army garrisoned on \Nplains from spring to summer,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.02,0:09:30.24,Thinking,,0,0,0,,with sweltering heat making access to water difficult and the wait miserable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.93,0:10:40.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.46,0:10:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}We taunt and curse them daily,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.33,0:10:45.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}yet the Wu army holds their positions.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.54,0:10:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}From spring to summer, Lu Xun \Nhas not engaged even once.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.19,0:10:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.433}He also ordered his troops to\N stuff their ears, declining to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.29,0:10:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Lu Xun, that whelp, has been scared out of his wits.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.50,0:11:06.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep fanning!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.28,0:11:10.48,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Lu Xun knows tactics well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.48,0:11:14.79,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He stalls as you attack from afar. \NHe is planning something.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.10,0:11:20.94,Default,,0,0,0,,He is waiting for something to happen in our army. \NPlease keep this in mind, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.73,0:11:25.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What stratagems could he have? \NThere is only cowardice.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.38,0:11:31.12,Default,,0,0,0,,The Wu army has suffered many defeats. How could they attack again?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.12,0:11:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,But-
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.24,0:11:33.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.74,0:11:38.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4700,5020)\pos(307.989,485.234)}Féng Xí\NStyled: Xiūyuán
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.58,0:11:37.25,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,The weather is scorching;\N the garrison feels as if they are in flames.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.25,0:11:39.40,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Obtaining water is difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.81,0:11:49.64,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Order to all garrisons: Move camp into the lush hills.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.64,0:11:53.51,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Stay close to streams and gullies to avoid the heat.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.89,0:11:56.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait to join forces and advance after autumn.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.85,0:11:57.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.83,0:12:02.56,Default,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.50,0:12:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,His Majesty's orders! Move camp into the lush hills!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.57,0:12:16.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Stay close to streams and gullies to avoid the heat!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.95,0:12:49.41,Thinking,,0,0,0,,After we camp into the hills,\N then should the Wu army attack...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.97,0:13:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Water! There's a river up ahead!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.93,0:13:52.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Quick, there's a river up ahead! Quick!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.64,0:14:07.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Cool water!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.81,0:14:28.36,Default,,0,0,0,,His Majesty is here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.36,0:14:33.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.37,0:14:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Rise, soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.33,0:14:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.19,0:14:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Go now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.38,0:14:47.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.89,0:15:10.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.84,0:15:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Your Majesty, our camp could be attacked at any time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.98,0:15:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I hope Your Majesty is well prepared.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.86,0:15:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}We have ordered eight thousand \Nelite soldiers to lay an ambush in the valleys.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.96,0:15:33.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Wu Ban is also leading our oldest soldiers \Nto camp near the Wu army.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.58,0:15:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Should Lu Xun learn of our movements, \Nhe would charge at Wu Ban,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.38,0:15:40.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}who would then feign retreat \Nand distract the Wu army.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.19,0:15:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}We would then ambush them from behind
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.38,0:15:45.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}and thus eliminate Lu Xun in one move.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.43,0:16:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.38,0:16:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Have the camps been arranged?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.07,0:16:11.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, the camps have been arranged.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.26,0:16:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Anything from the Wu army?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.94,0:16:14.62,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(377.748,444)}Guān Xīng\NStyled: Ānguó
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.90,0:16:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,No reports of the Wu Army.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.80,0:16:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Good!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.05,0:16:27.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, the Shu army went into the forested hills.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.10,0:16:30.34,Default,,0,0,0,,They set up camp next to water and shade.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.34,0:16:31.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Now is our chance to strike!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.92,0:16:33.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Please come with me to take a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.99,0:16:34.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.03,0:16:46.66,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Fighting these old men will be child's play.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.66,0:16:48.96,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I can attack in two directions with General Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.96,0:16:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,If we fail, we welcome punishment by military law!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.01,0:16:51.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.32,0:16:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Look! That valley looks ominous.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.88,0:16:58.06,Default,,0,0,0,,There must be an ambush there.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.17,0:17:03.35,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Liu Bei placed those weak troops \Non flat ground to lure us.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.35,0:17:05.38,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Officers, do not sally forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.70,0:17:13.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.17,0:17:18.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor Zhuge is inspecting the chokepoints of the Eastern Riverlands in case of a Wei incursion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.75,0:17:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not draw a map of the camp \Nand send it to him for guidance?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.25,0:17:26.51,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Fine, fine. But I can handle military strategy myself, \Nso this will just bother him.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.79,0:17:28.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Enough. Speak no more.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.65,0:17:38.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The Shu camp is quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.81,0:17:40.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Look!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.84,0:18:05.58,Default,,0,0,0,,An ambush indeed. What incredible foresight, Commander!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.58,0:18:08.93,Default,,0,0,0,,This is why I forbade you from attacking.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.32,0:18:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that the ambush is gone, \NShu will be defeated in ten days.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.42,0:18:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,We should have struck when they were shifting camp. How can we strike now that they are secure?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.49,0:18:23.92,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Liu Bei is a mighty and cunning raptor.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.92,0:18:28.02,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,When Shu drew first blood, \Nthey were focused and disciplined.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.43,0:18:31.36,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Now, after fighting for so long without a victory,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.36,0:18:34.93,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,their soldiers will be exhausted. \NThus, today will be the fall of Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.70,0:18:43.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a plan to defeat Shu. I will present it to the king.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.04,0:19:06.61,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Now that the land produced a genius\N like Lu Xun, what worries could I have?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.22,0:19:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}The camps are moved to straddle the river, \Noccupying over seven hundred {\i1}li{\i0} in width.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.34,0:19:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}More than forty camps were set up,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.15,0:19:41.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}all on land next to streams and dense woods.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.17,0:19:46.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}The Emperor ordered me to present\N this map to you, Chancellor, for viewing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.50,0:19:55.74,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4900,5220)\pos(295.529,461.333)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.64,0:19:55.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Who let the Emperor set up camp thus?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.52,0:19:58.87,Default,,0,0,0,,This man must be executed!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.18,0:20:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the Emperor's own plan, not that of anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.15,0:20:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did you not object?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.08,0:20:11.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The Emperor did not listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.71,0:20:39.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The great Han Dynasty...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.26,0:20:42.97,Default,,0,0,0,,is doomed.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.04,0:20:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}To camp amidst thickets, humidity, and obstacles,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.12,0:21:04.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}these are all grave taboos of military leadership.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.06,0:21:08.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}If Lu Xun were to strike with fire, what then?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.36,0:21:19.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}What use is there to set up camps\N for seven hundred {\i1}li{\i0} against an enemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.68,0:21:26.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Disaster will come soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.53,0:21:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei is about to be defeated!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.22,0:21:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, how will Liu Bei be defeated?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.30,0:21:36.82,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Liu Xuande knows nothing of military strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.82,0:21:40.21,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,How can stretching camps over \Nseven hundred {\i1}li{\i0} deter a foe?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.54,0:21:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Garrisoning in irregular, dense forests is a classic sin of military strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.00,0:21:51.50,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Liu Bei will be defeated by the hands of \NLu Xun of Eastern Wu within ten days.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.22,0:22:00.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,5500,5860)\pos(814.925,490.667)}Cáo Rén\NStyled: Zǐxiào
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.36,0:21:57.46,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, as a precautionary measure,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.46,0:22:00.53,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,please allot troops to remain on guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.53,0:22:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed. Your Majesty, please allot\N troops to be vigilant for sudden changes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.86,0:22:13.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,6860,7220)\pos(864.179,485.334)}Cáo Pī\NStyled: Zǐhuán
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.50,0:22:11.87,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, should Lu Xun be victorious, \Nhe will aim for the Western Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.87,0:22:14.85,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,The Wu army would be far away, leaving their realm empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.85,0:22:17.94,Default,,0,0,0,,We would then pretend to assist with our soldiers,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.09,0:22:23.65,Default,,0,0,0,,ordering our three armies to advance together. Thus, Eastern Wu shall be ours!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.92,0:22:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Brilliantly said, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.42,0:22:29.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Jichang.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.70,0:22:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.52,0:22:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Go back to Yiling to tell the Emperor\N to move camp. This is unacceptable.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.37,0:22:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Wu army is victorious, what should be done?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.42,0:22:52.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Lu Xun will not dare to give chase. Chengdu is safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.15,0:22:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Why will Lu Xun not give chase?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.74,0:23:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}He fears an invasion from Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.14,0:23:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Should anything happen to\N the Emperor, he should retreat to Baidi.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.02,0:23:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}When I entered the Riverlands,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.69,0:23:13.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}I laid an ambush of a hundred\N thousand elite troops at Yufupu.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.58,0:23:19.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Yufupu? A hundred thousand troops?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.54,0:23:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I have passed through Yufupu many times,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.02,0:23:26.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}yet I have not seen a single soldier. \NWhy do you say "a hundred thousand"?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.05,0:23:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}You will see them on your way. Ask no more.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.00,0:23:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Go back to Yiling, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.54,0:23:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I will return to Chengdu to arrange troops in support.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.04,0:23:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.91,0:23:37.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhu Ran, orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.40,0:23:38.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.29,0:23:42.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Advance by water. When the\N southeastern winds start tomorrow night,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.07,0:23:45.76,Default,,0,0,0,,load your ships with straw and act as we planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.76,0:23:46.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.30,0:23:47.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Han Dang, orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.66,0:23:48.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.37,0:23:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Lead an army to attack the northern bank of the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.78,0:23:52.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.71,0:23:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhou Tai, orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.90,0:23:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.69,0:23:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Lead an army to attack the southern bank of the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.94,0:23:59.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.14,0:24:04.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Each army shall bring their own kindling and arms, and advance together.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.53,0:24:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,At the Shu camp, raise the torches with the wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.70,0:24:13.10,Default,,0,0,0,,The Shu army has forty encampments. \NBurn only twenty; set every other camp on fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.10,0:24:14.85,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Each man shall bring their own supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.85,0:24:19.49,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Do not withdraw until Liu Bei is captured!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.49,0:24:20.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.82,0:24:34.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Go.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.41,0:24:54.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I saw Wu troops \Nmoving east along the mountains.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.16,0:24:58.76,Default,,0,0,0,,That is a ruse. The army will stay here.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.44,0:25:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Guan Xing and Zhang Bao.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.61,0:25:03.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.38,0:25:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I order you two to lead 500 cavalrymen to patrol.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.00,0:25:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.92,0:27:36.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, the camps north of the river are on fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.57,0:27:51.25,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,You two, go scout both sides of the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.25,0:27:52.89,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Report should there be Wu troops!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.89,0:27:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.19,0:28:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.08,0:28:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.54,0:28:14.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! The left garrison\N of the imperial camp is on fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.96,0:28:16.38,Default,,0,0,0,,-Put out the fire!\N-Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.38,0:28:20.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Report! Your Majesty, the right garrison\N of the imperial camp is on fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.74,0:28:28.74,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(650.756,80.597)}Destroy Eastern Wu
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.70,0:30:27.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.85,0:30:47.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.78,0:31:44.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.26,0:31:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Fire, fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.55,0:31:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.45,0:31:58.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:59.09,0:32:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, this place is called Ma'anshan.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.16,0:32:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, Lu Xun has surrounded\N this mountain. We cannot stay for long.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:09.34,0:32:12.36,Default,,0,0,0,,You should go to Baidi and gather forces there.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.51,0:32:17.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Who can cover our retreat?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.74,0:32:21.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I am willing to cover the retreat to my death.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.53,0:32:48.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:54.31,0:32:57.69,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, General Fu Tong, \Nwhile covering the retreat,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.69,0:33:00.18,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,was swarmed and died in battle!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.18,0:33:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,The Wu army is catching up!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.05,0:33:06.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Order the men to remove their armor
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.22,0:33:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}and burn them on the road to stop them!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.45,0:33:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.46,0:33:32.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(889.456,421.333)}Yúfù Shore
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.42,0:33:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks ominous up ahead. There must be an ambush.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.94,0:33:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Generals, come with me to scout ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.28,0:35:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,We've fallen for Zhuge Liang's trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.30,0:35:14.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,750,4700,5020)\pos(482.241,424)}Huáng Chéngyàn
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.76,0:35:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,General, do you wish to exit this formation?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.27,0:35:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder, please lead the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:22.49,0:35:24.43,Default,,0,0,0,,General, follow me.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.44,0:35:45.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder, where did you come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.40,0:35:52.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I am Zhuge Kongming's father-in-law,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.15,0:35:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Huang Chengyan.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.85,0:35:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}When my son-in-law entered the Riverlands,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.09,0:36:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}he made this formation of stones
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.76,0:36:05.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}and named it the "Eightfold Maze."
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.52,0:36:09.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}The eight gates move back\N and forth and change unpredictably.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.61,0:36:14.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}It is comparable to a hundred thousand elite troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:14.04,0:36:20.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}When Kongming was leaving, he instructed me:
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.45,0:36:24.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}"A general from Eastern Wu\N will be lost in the formation."
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.40,0:36:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}"You must not lead him out."
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.35,0:36:36.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Just now, I saw from the mountain
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.26,0:36:39.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}that you were entering through the "Gate of Death."
Dialogue: 0,0:36:39.44,0:36:44.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}I presumed you did not know\N this formation and would be lost in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.24,0:36:48.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I always prefer doing kind deeds,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.28,0:36:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}and do not want to see you get trapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.69,0:36:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}For this, I come to lead you out of the "Gate of Life."
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.17,0:36:55.96,Default,,0,0,0,,General, follow me.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:25.91,0:37:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the Elder? Where's the Elder?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.21,0:37:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,General!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.25,0:37:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder, would you be willing to teach me this formation?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:40.29,0:37:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It is infinitely variable and cannot be learned.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:49.25,0:37:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Go quickly, General. It is not\N advisable to continue the campaign.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.48,0:37:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Elder.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.07,0:38:11.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Kongming is truly a Sleeping Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.47,0:38:16.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I am no match for him! I am no match for him!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:16.16,0:38:18.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Withdraw! Withdraw!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.37,0:38:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}Commander, now that Liu Bei has lost his army
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.84,0:38:23.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}and is trapped in Baidi, this is our chance to strike.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.92,0:38:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}How can we withdraw due to a rock \Nformation, failing at the cusp of success?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.32,0:38:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I do not fear the rock formation.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.31,0:38:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}I fear that the cunning Lord of Wei, Cao Pi,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.25,0:38:38.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746\pos(640,666)}will exploit our campaign to invade our Jiangdong.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.79,0:38:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.746}Should I enter deep into the Riverlands, I would be unable to guard against Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.31,0:39:37.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty...

